ype."},"34":{"id":"/docs/api/adapter-builder-32","page_id":"/docs/api/adapter-builder","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/adapter-builder#transform","content":"The `transform` hook allows you to modify the event data before it is sent to the tracking system. This hook is highly flexible, enabling you to change, enrich, or sanitize the event data according to your specific needs. It also supports scenarios where `RealEventData` is a mapped object of `EventData`."},"35":{"id":"/docs/api/adapter-builder-33","page_id":"/docs/api/adapter-builder","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/adapter-builder#parameters-2","content":"**eventType** : `keyof EventData | [keyof EventData, keyof RealEventData]`"},"36":{"id":"/docs/api/adapter-builder-34","page_id":"/docs/api/adapter-builder","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/adapter-builder#parameters-2","content":"The type of event being tracked. Typically, this is a key from the `EventData` that corresponds to specific events like click, purchase, etc. When `RealEventData` is used, it allows you to map the `EventData` to a corresponding event type in `RealEventData`."},"37":{"id":"/docs/api/adapter-builder-35","page_id":"/docs/api/adapter-builder","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/adapter-builder#parameters-2","content":"**fun** : `(\nctx: Context,\neventType: EventType,\neventData: EventData[keyof EventType]\n) => AdapterReportData | Promise<AdapterReportData>`"},"38":{"id":"/docs/api/adapter-builder-36","page_id":"/docs/api/adapter-builder","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/adapter-builder#parameters-2","content":"A function that transforms the event data. The function receives the event type and data, and should return the modified data, either directly or as a promise."},"39":{"id":"/docs/api/adapter-builder-37","page_id":"/docs/api/adapter-builder","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/adapter-builder#example-2","content":"The following examples illustrate how to use the `transform` hook to modi