he new license aims to balance the needs of open-source community use with the commercial sustainability of the project."},"189":{"id":"/docs/faq-4","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq","content":"This change includes specifics on usage rights, redistribution, and potential costs for commercial entities. More information please see LICENSE"},"190":{"id":"/docs/faq-5","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq","content":"Do I need to pay for Track now?"},"191":{"id":"/docs/faq-6","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq","content":"Usually you can use the open source version, This version is for long-term maintenance, which is free of charge."},"192":{"id":"/docs/faq-7","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq","content":"However we also provide some highly packaged plugins to facilitate rapid business integration, If you use these plug-ins. A small fee is required."},"193":{"id":"/docs/faq-8","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq","content":"What is Hyperse?"},"194":{"id":"/docs/faq-9","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq","content":"Leveraging a cutting-edge, robust open-source full-stack core, we deliver comprehensive and innovative architectural solutions and expert consulting services for medium to large tech enterprises. Our offerings encompass advanced front-end, back-end, big data, Android, and iOS technologies. Additionally, we specialize in crafting bespoke e-commerce platform solutions, tailored to meet the unique needs of your business."},"195":{"id":"/docs/faq-10","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq","content":"More information please see Hyperse"},"196":{"id":"/docs/guide","page_id":"/docs/guide","type":"page","content":"Guide","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Guide"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/guide"},"197":{"id":"/docs/guide-0","page_id":"/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide","content":"Getting started with Hyperse Track."},"198":{"id":"/docs/guide-1","page_id":"/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide","content":"New to Track? Start with **Introduction**, install the package, then try the\nsample and live examples."},"199":{"id":"/docs/guide-2","page_id":"/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide","content":"<Card title=\"Introduction\" href=\"/guide/introduction\" />"},"200":{"id":"/docs/guide-3","page_id":"/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide","content":"<Card title=\"Installation\" href=\"/guide/installation\" />"},"201":{"id":"/docs/guide-4","page_id":"/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide","content":"<Card title=\"Sample Example\" href=\"/guide/sample-example\" />"},"202":{"id":"/docs/guide-5","page_id":"/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide","content":"<Card title=\"Live Example\" href=\"/guide/live-example\" />"},"203":{"id":"/docs/guide/installation","page_id":"/docs/guide/installation","type":"page","content":"Installation","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Guide","Installation"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/guide/installation"},"204":{"id":"/docs/guide/installation-0","page_id":"/docs/guide/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guide/installation#requirements","content":"Requirements"},"205":{"id":"/docs/guide/installation-1","page_id":"/docs/guide/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guide/installation#install","content":"Install"},"206":{"id":"/docs/guide/installation-2","page_id":"/docs/guide/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guide/installation#congratulations-","content":"Congratulations !"},"207":{"id":"/docs/guide/installation-3","page_id":"/docs/guide/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide/installation#requirements","content":"Node.js v18 or above, with support for even-numbered Node.js versions."},"208":{"id":"/docs/guide/installation-4","page_id":"/docs/guide/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide/installation#install","content":"We have completed installing the package."},"209":{"id":"/docs/guide/installation-5","page_id":"/docs/guide/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide/installation#congratulations-","content":"That's all, now let's deep dive into the props."},"210":{"id":"/docs/guide/introduction","page_id":"/docs/guide/introduction","type":"page","content":"Introducing Track","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Guide","Introducing Track"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/guide/introduction"},"211":{"id":"/docs/guide/introduction-0","page_id":"/docs/guide/introduction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guide/introduction#what-is-track-","content":"What is Track ?"},"212":{"id":"/docs/guide/introduction-1","page_id":"/docs/guide/introduction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guide/introduction#track-a-modern-typescript-library-for-data-collection","content":"Track: A Modern TypeScript Library for Data Collection"},"213":{"id":"/docs/guide/introduction-2","page_id":"/docs/guide/introduction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guide/introduction#key-features-of-track","content":"Key Features of Track"},"214":{"id":"/docs/guide/introduction-3","page_id":"/docs/guide/introduction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guide/introduction#use-cases-for-track","content":"Use Cases for Track"},"215":{"id":"/docs/guide/introduction-4","page_id":"/docs/guide/introduction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guide/introduction#congratulations-","content":"Congratulations !"},"216":{"id":"/docs/guide/introduction-5","page_id":"/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide/introduction#track-a-modern-typescript-library-for-data-collection","content":"**Track** is a sophisticated TypeScript library designed specifically for efficient and versatile data collection in web applications. With a focus on modern development practices, Track incorporates several powerful features, making it an ideal choice for developers seeking a reliable and scalable solution for front-end data tracking."},"217":{"id":"/docs/guide/introduction-6","page_id":"/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide/introduction#key-features-of-track","content":"**TypeScript-Based Development**:"},"218":{"id":"/docs/guide/introduction-7","page_id":"/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide/introduction#key-features-of-track","content":"**Track** is built using TypeScript, which provides strong typing and advanced development tools. This ensures that developers can catch errors during development, resulting in more reliable and maintainable code."},"219":{"id":"/docs/guide/introduction-8","page_id":"/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide/introduction#key-features-of-track","content":"**Strong Typing and Type Inference**:"},"220":{"id":"/docs/guide/introduction-9","page_id":"/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide/introduction#key-features-of-track","content":"Track fully supports TypeScript's type inference, allowing developers to benefit from strong typing without having to manually specify types everywhere. This reduces runtime errors and improves overall code stability."},"221":{"id":"/docs/guide/introduction-10","page_id":"/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide/introduction#key-features-of-track","content":"**Smart Data Collection**:"},"222":{"id":"/docs/guide/introduction-11","page_id":"/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide/introduction#key-features-of-track","content":"Track integrates intelligent data collection strategies that optimize the process based on user behavior and changing data. This ensures that the data collected is both accurate and timely, without overloading the front-end application."},"223":{"id":"/docs/guide/introduction-12","page_id":"/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide/introduction#key-features-of-track","content":"**Scalable Design**:"},"224":{"id":"/docs/guide/introduction-13","page_id":"/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide/introduction#key-features-of-track","content":"Whether you're working on a small project or a large-scale application, Track is designed to scale effortlessly. Its architecture supports the collection of vast amounts of data without compromising performance, making it suitable for applications of all sizes."},"225":{"id":"/docs/guide/introduction-14","page_id":"/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide/introduction#key-features-of-track","content":"**Powerful and Flexible**:"},"226":{"id":"/docs/guide/introduction-15","page_id":"/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide/introduction#key-features-of-track","content":"Track is equipped with a robust set of features that allow it to handle a wide variety of data sources. From DOM elements to user inputs and network requests, Track can collect and process data from multiple sources with ease. Its flexibility allows developers to customize collection parameters, such as frequency, format, and filtering rules, to meet specific application needs."},"227":{"id":"/docs/guide/introduction-16","page_id":"/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide/introduction#key-features-of-track","content":"**Front-End Focused**:"},"228":{"id":"/docs/guide/introduction-17","page_id":"/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide/introduction#key-features-of-track","content":"Designed with the front-end in mind, Track is lightweight and optimized for performance. It collects data efficiently without affecting the user experience, making it an excellent choice for modern web applications where performance is critical."},"229":{"id":"/docs/guide/introduction-18","page_id":"/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide/introduction#key-features-of-track","content":"**Easy Integration**:"},"230":{"id":"/docs/guide/introduction-19","page_id":"/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide/introduction#key-features-of-track","content":"Track provides an intuitive API that seamlessly integrates with popular front-end frameworks like React, Vue, and Angular. This makes it easy to add data collection capabilities to existing projects without disrupting the current workflow."},"231":{"id":"/docs/guide/introduction-20","page_id":"/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide/introduction#use-cases-for-track","content":"**User Behavior Analysis**: Track can be used to gather detailed information about how users interact with your web application. By tracking clicks, scrolls, form submissions, and other actions, you can gain insights into user behavior and optimize your application accordingly."},"232":{"id":"/docs/guide/introduction-21","page_id":"/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide/introduction#use-cases-for-track","content":"**Performance Monitoring**: Track allows you to monitor the performance of your web application in real-time. By collecting data on page load times, resource usage, and other metrics, you can quickly identify and address performance bottlenecks."},"233":{"id":"/docs/guide/introduction-22","page_id":"/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide/introduction#use-cases-for-track","content":"**A/B Testing**: With Track, you can easily implement A/B testing by collecting data from different versions of your web pages. This helps you make data-driven decisions by comparing how users interact with each version."},"234":{"id":"/docs/guide/introduction-23","page_id":"/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide/introduction#use-cases-for-track","content":"**Event Tracking**: Track makes it easy to set up custom event tracking in your application. Whether you need to monitor specific user actions or track conversions, Track provides the tools you need to capture and analyze the data."},"235":{"id":"/docs/guide/introduction-24","page_id":"/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide/introduction#congratulations-","content":"That's all, now let's deep dive into the BaseAdapter."},"236":{"id":"/docs/guide/live-example","page_id":"/docs/guide/live-example","type":"page","content":"Live Example","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Guide","Live Example"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/guide/live-example"},"237":{"id":"/docs/guide/live-example-0","page_id":"/docs/guide/live-example","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guide/live-example#live-usage","content":"Live usage"},"238":{"id":"/docs/guide/live-example-1","page_id":"/docs/guide/live-example","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guide/live-example#congratulations","content":"Congratulations!"},"239":{"id":"/docs/guide/live-example-2","page_id":"/docs/guide/live-example","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide/live-example#live-usage","content":"Below is the complete usage of the component, representing a real business scenario:"},"240":{"id":"/docs/guide/live-example-3","page_id":"/docs/guide/live-example","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide/live-example#live-usage","content":"Read more in User guide → Introduction"},"241":{"id":"/docs/guide/live-example-4","page_id":"/docs/guide/live-example","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guide/live-example#congratulations","content":"That's all, now let's deep dive into the API."},"242":{"id":"/docs/guide/sample-example","page_id":"/docs/guide/sample-example","type":"page","content":"Sample Example","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Guide","Sample Example"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/guide/sample-example"},"243":{"id":"/docs/guide/sample-example-0","page_id":"/docs/guide/sample-example","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guide/sample-example#simple-usage","content":"Simple usage"}